# Files not uploaded to Vercel.
#
# This controls the upload, which the build then runs against — so anything the
# build needs has to stay. `frontend/src` is not listed for exactly that reason:
# `scripts/vercel-build.sh` compiles it, and without the sources there is
# nothing to compile.
#
# What is listed is either reinstalled during the build, or never read at
# runtime. The function has a 250 MB unzipped limit and the dependencies already
# take about 200 MB, so the margin is worth protecting.

# Reinstalled by the build
frontend/node_modules/
node_modules/

# Local environments
.venv*/
venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# The local database. Postgres is required in production — settings.py refuses
# to start on a serverless host without DATABASE_URL — so this would only be
# confusing to find in the bundle.
db.sqlite3
*.sqlite3

# Nothing imports these at runtime.
**/tests.py
**/tests_*.py
docs/
.claude/

# Other deployment targets
Procfile
nixpacks.toml
requirements-asgi.txt

# Version control and editors
.git/
.github/
.vscode/
.idea/
